course: dictionary
lesson: 15819
title: Formal words: unconsumed
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unconsumed is a formal word. It means not eaten, not drunk, or not used up. The start un- means not, and consumed means eaten or used up, so unconsumed means not yet used up. «The bowl of soup was still full, so the soup was unconsumed.»
explain: Science and money texts use this word often. «The engine burned only half the petrol, so the rest was unconsumed fuel.» Fuel is unconsumed when it was never burned. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap in an everyday word such as unused or left over, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: In everyday talk, people say «uneaten», «unused» or «left over» instead. «The school sent home unconsumed sandwiches» means the sandwiches came back still uneaten. Formal words are often a more exact way of saying something, so keep your everyday words for chatting and learn these for writing.
fact: Unconsumed means not eaten, drunk or used up.
fact: Unconsumed can describe fuel or energy that was not burned or used.
fact: «Unconsumed food» means food that was left over and not eaten.
fact: «Unconsumed fuel» means fuel that was not burned.
fact: In everyday talk, use «uneaten», «unused» or «left over» instead.
exercise: «The lunch box came home with unconsumed sandwiches inside.» What does unconsumed mean here? | Eaten very fast | Packed in a box | Cold and wet | *Not eaten
exercise: «Only some of the petrol was burned, so the unconsumed fuel stayed in the tank.» What is unconsumed fuel? | *Fuel that was not burned or used | Fuel that has been spilt on the road | Fuel that was never burned | Fuel that was burned very quickly
exercise: «The unconsumed cake was kept for Sunday.» Find and copy the word that means not eaten. | cake | *unconsumed | Sunday | kept
test: Which everyday word is the best swap for unconsumed in «unconsumed food»? | frozen | *uneaten, meaning not eaten | uneaten | hot
test: Which everyday word could replace unconsumed in «unconsumed fuel»? | bright | loud | sweet | *unused
exam: «The unconsumed fuel was saved for the winter.» Why might a scientist mention unconsumed fuel? | It was fuel that exploded | It was fuel bought at the shop | *It was fuel that was not burned | It was fuel that was wet
